  "labin-republic": {
   "story": "On 7 March 1921, during a strike by about two thousand miners at the Arsa coal mines in Labin, in Istria (then newly annexed by Italy), the miners occupied the mines and proclaimed a republic under the slogan 'Kova je nasa' (the mine is ours). The strike followed attacks by fascists on a union in Trieste and the beating of the strike leader Giovanni Pippan. Miners formed a red guard and ran production themselves with some farmers' support. On 8 April Italian authorities sent a thousand soldiers at the owners' request and ended it. Fifty-two miners were indicted and a jury acquitted them.",
